//! leaks: 2 blocked on channel_recv
// Two of them, so the count is checked and not just the wording.
//
// This case caught a real undercount: threads used to register themselves from
// inside the spawned domain, so `spawn` returned before the entry existed and a
// main that spawns and exits could reach the report first. It read "1 blocked
// on channel_recv" on a loaded runner -- and an undercount is the bad direction
// for a leak report, because fewer leaks looks like a cleaner program. The
// parent registers now. Delay the child's first instruction to see the old
// behaviour.
let ch = channel_new ();
let _a = spawn (fn () -> let _ = channel_recv ch in ());
let _b = spawn (fn () -> let _ = channel_recv ch in ());
print "parent done"
